WEBVTT

1
00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:22.457
They ought to make the day the time
changes, the first day of summer.

2
00:02:22.537 --> 00:02:23.317
What?

3
00:02:23.397 --> 00:02:25.868
Well, it's 8 o'clock and it's still light.

4
00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:28.417
A lot of good the extra daylight does us.

5
00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:30.697
Now, we've still got a
three-hour drive back.

6
00:02:30.777 --> 00:02:32.497
We're not going to be
home until after midnight.

7
00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:35.257
Well, if it really bugged you,
Johnny, you wouldn't do it.

8
00:02:35.337 --> 00:02:38.277
You think I want to blow
Sunday on a scene like this?

9
00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:41.617
You know, I figure we're either going to
have to move Mother out here or move the

10
00:02:41.697 --> 00:02:42.877
grave into Pittsburgh.

11
00:02:42.957 --> 00:02:45.217
She can't make a trip like this.

12
00:02:45.417 --> 00:02:47.097
I know that she can't.

13
00:02:47.177 --> 00:02:49.137
Is there any of that candy left?

14
00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.517
No.

15
00:02:51.597 --> 00:02:53.437
Look at this thing. We still remember.

16
00:02:53.517 --> 00:02:56.877
I don't. You know, I don't even
remember what the man looks like.

17
00:02:56.957 --> 00:02:58.877
Johnny, it takes you five minutes.

18
00:02:58.957 --> 00:03:02.757
Yeah, five minutes to put the wreath on
the grave and six hours to drive back and

19
00:03:02.837 --> 00:03:03.657
forth.

20
00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:07.957
Mother wants to remember, so we trot 200
miles into the country and she stays at

21
00:03:08.037 --> 00:03:10.597
home. Well, we're here, John, all right?

22
00:03:12.837 --> 00:03:14.337
Oh, Tessie.

23
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:15.557
Back on?

24
00:03:15.637 --> 00:03:16.637
Oh.

25
00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:21.717
Uh, ladies and gentlemen, we're coming
back on the air after an interruption due to

26
00:03:21.797 --> 00:03:23.197
technical problems.

27
00:03:35.337 --> 00:03:37.017
Nothing wrong with the radio.

28
00:03:37.097 --> 00:03:38.517
Must have been the station.

29
00:03:38.597 --> 00:03:40.237
Which row is it in?

30
00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:47.157
I'm sorry.

31
00:04:00.737 --> 00:04:02.737
Well, there's no one around.

32
00:04:02.877 --> 00:04:05.657
Well, it's late. You'd gotten up earlier.

33
00:04:05.737 --> 00:04:08.617
Oh, look, I already lost an
hour's sleep on the time change.

34
00:04:08.697 --> 00:04:11.777
I think you complain just
to hear yourself talk.

35
00:04:12.097 --> 00:04:13.437
There it is.

36
00:04:29.317 --> 00:04:32.237
I wonder what happened
to the one from last year.

37
00:04:33.057 --> 00:04:35.597
Each year we spend good
money on these things.

38
00:04:35.677 --> 00:04:38.617
We come out here and the
one from last year is gone.

39
00:04:38.697 --> 00:04:43.277
Well, the flowers die and the
caretaker or somebody takes them away.

40
00:04:43.577 --> 00:04:45.077
Yeah, a little spit and polish.

41
00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:46.497
You can clean this up.

42
00:04:46.817 --> 00:04:48.517
Sell it next year.

43
00:04:48.717 --> 00:04:51.482
I wonder how many times
we bought the same one.

44
00:05:08.697 --> 00:05:11.579
Hey, come on, Barb.
Church was this morning, huh?

45
00:05:30.497 --> 00:05:33.037
Hey, I mean, praying's for church, huh?

46
00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:34.257
Come on.

47
00:05:35.057 --> 00:05:37.537
I haven't seen you in church lately.

48
00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:42.017
There's not much sense
in my going to church.

49
00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:46.277
Do you remember one time when
we were small, we were out here?

50
00:05:46.357 --> 00:05:48.317
It was from right over there.

51
00:05:48.397 --> 00:05:51.797
I jumped out at you from behind the
tree, and Grandpa got all excited,

52
00:05:51.877 --> 00:05:56.057
and he shook his fist at me, and he
said, Boy, you'll be damned to hell.

53
00:05:56.137 --> 00:05:58.137
Remember that? Right over there.

54
00:05:58.877 --> 00:06:01.230
Well, you used to really be scared here.

55
00:06:02.017 --> 00:06:03.017
Johnny.

56
00:06:03.397 --> 00:06:05.037
You're still afraid.

57
00:06:05.217 --> 00:06:07.177
Stop it now. I mean it.

58
00:06:10.857 --> 00:06:13.897
They're coming to get you, Barbara.

59
00:06:14.497 --> 00:06:16.937
Stop it. You're ignorant.

60
00:06:17.017 --> 00:06:19.337
They're coming for you, Barbara.

61
00:06:19.817 --> 00:06:22.337
Stop it. You're acting like a child.

62
00:06:22.417 --> 00:06:24.217
They're coming for you.

63
00:06:24.597 --> 00:06:27.217
Look, there comes one of them now.

64
00:06:27.997 --> 00:06:30.377
He'll hear you. Here he comes now.

65
00:06:30.457 --> 00:06:32.517
I'm getting out of here. Johnny.

66
00:06:39.017 --> 00:06:41.597
Oh, no!

67
00:06:42.757 --> 00:06:44.577
Johnny,

68
00:06:44.877 --> 00:06:46.217
help me!

69
00:07:08.697 --> 00:07:09.697
Let's go.

70
00:07:51.357 --> 00:07:54.777
Oh, my God.

71
00:08:19.797 --> 00:08:23.097
Oh, my God.

72
00:08:50.437 --> 00:08:52.857
Come on.

73
00:12:08.377 --> 00:12:11.677
I'm sorry.

74
00:13:17.657 --> 00:13:18.677
No!

75
00:13:47.657 --> 00:13:48.657
Shh.

76
00:13:55.217 --> 00:13:56.397
It's all right.

77
00:14:00.337 --> 00:14:02.117
Don't worry about him, I can handle him.

78
00:14:02.197 --> 00:14:05.962
Probably be a lot more of him as
soon as they find out about us.

79
00:14:08.677 --> 00:14:10.097
Truck is out of gas.

80
00:14:10.177 --> 00:14:12.824
This pump out here is
locked, is there a key?

81
00:14:13.957 --> 00:14:17.637
We can try to get out here if we
can get some gas, is there a key?

82
00:14:17.717 --> 00:14:19.117
Oh, my God.

83
00:14:26.697 --> 00:14:28.677
I suppose you've tried this.

84
00:14:38.617 --> 00:14:40.157
Do you live here?

85
00:14:53.957 --> 00:14:54.957
Jesus.

86
00:15:03.597 --> 00:15:05.303
We've got to get out of here.

87
00:15:05.517 --> 00:15:08.458
We have to get to where
there's some other people.

88
00:15:11.337 --> 00:15:13.278
Maybe we'd better take some food.

89
00:15:13.917 --> 00:15:15.858
I'll see if I can find some food.

90
00:16:00.177 --> 00:16:02.217
What's happening?

91
00:16:02.337 --> 00:16:03.857
What's happening?

92
00:16:19.457 --> 00:16:20.677
Two of them.

93
00:16:25.997 --> 00:16:27.277
There are two of them out there.

94
00:16:27.357 --> 00:16:28.837
Have you seen any more around here?

95
00:16:28.917 --> 00:16:30.337
I can take care of those two.

96
00:16:30.417 --> 00:16:32.637
I don't know. I know you're
afraid, but we have to...

97
00:16:32.717 --> 00:16:34.077
I don't know!

98
00:16:34.157 --> 00:16:35.497
I don't know!

99
00:16:36.337 --> 00:16:37.757
What's happening?

100
00:16:49.277 --> 00:16:51.997
Oh, my God.

101
00:17:17.537 --> 00:17:19.597
Come on.

102
00:17:58.457 --> 00:18:02.017
Oh, my God.

103
00:18:36.657 --> 00:18:40.117
Oh, no, no.

104
00:18:55.957 --> 00:18:57.837
I know we're in here now.

105
00:19:12.937 --> 00:19:14.417
Don't look at it.

106
00:19:55.957 --> 00:19:56.957
Thank you.

107
00:20:27.397 --> 00:20:29.632
Get some more lights on in this house.

108
00:21:08.357 --> 00:21:10.317
We'll find some wood, some board,
something about it far up here.

109
00:21:10.397 --> 00:21:12.515
Something we can nail this place up.

110
00:21:17.877 --> 00:21:18.877
Goddamn!

111
00:21:22.637 --> 00:21:24.797
Look, I know you're afraid.

112
00:21:24.997 --> 00:21:26.457
I'm afraid too.

113
00:21:27.117 --> 00:21:29.937
But we have to try to
board the house up together.

114
00:21:30.017 --> 00:21:32.317
Now, I'm going to board up
the windows and the doors.

115
00:21:32.397 --> 00:21:33.137
Do you understand?

116
00:21:33.217 --> 00:21:34.797
We'll be all right here.

117
00:21:34.937 --> 00:21:38.277
We'll be all right here until
someone comes to rescue us.

118
00:21:38.357 --> 00:21:41.677
You'll have to help me. Now, I want you
to go in and get some wood so I can board

119
00:21:41.757 --> 00:21:43.617
the place up. Do you understand?

120
00:21:43.697 --> 00:21:44.697
OK?

121
00:21:45.657 --> 00:21:46.657
OK?

122
00:22:55.937 --> 00:22:56.937
Come on.

123
00:23:22.457 --> 00:23:24.397
Come on.

124
00:24:25.817 --> 00:24:28.137
I'm not that strong.

125
00:24:28.477 --> 00:24:29.537
Why don't you pick out something else?

126
00:24:29.617 --> 00:24:31.911
Pick out the biggest ones you can find.

127
00:24:36.897 --> 00:24:39.073
There, this room looks pretty secure.

128
00:24:41.837 --> 00:24:45.190
If we have to, we can run in
here and board up the doors.

129
00:24:47.617 --> 00:24:50.177
Won't be long for those days to
be back pounding their way in here.

130
00:24:50.257 --> 00:24:51.497
They're afraid now.

131
00:24:56.237 --> 00:24:58.649
They're afraid of fire. I found that out.

132
00:25:10.557 --> 00:25:13.497
You know a place back down
the road called Beatman's?

133
00:25:13.577 --> 00:25:14.777
Beatman's Diner?

134
00:25:21.717 --> 00:25:25.070
Anyhow, that's where I found
that truck I have out there.

135
00:25:26.877 --> 00:25:28.677
There's a radio in the truck.

136
00:25:29.917 --> 00:25:32.257
I had jumped in to listen to it...

137
00:25:32.817 --> 00:25:36.557
when a big gasoline truck came
screaming right across the road...

138
00:25:36.637 --> 00:25:41.117
where there must have been 10,
15 of those things chasing after it.

139
00:25:42.197 --> 00:25:43.777
Grabbing and holding on.

140
00:25:47.157 --> 00:25:49.017
I didn't see them at first.

141
00:25:50.997 --> 00:25:54.409
I could just see that the
truck was moving in a funny way.

142
00:25:54.837 --> 00:25:56.977
Those things were catching up to it.

143
00:25:59.697 --> 00:26:02.517
The truck went right across the road.

144
00:26:04.017 --> 00:26:06.997
I slammed down my brakes to
keep from hitting it myself.

145
00:26:07.077 --> 00:26:09.237
It went right through the guardrail.

146
00:26:14.097 --> 00:26:15.557
I guess...

147
00:26:16.017 --> 00:26:21.417
I guess the driver must have cut off the
road into that gas station by Beekman's

148
00:26:21.497 --> 00:26:22.497
Diner.

149
00:26:23.337 --> 00:26:26.777
It went right through the
billboard, ripped over a gas pump,

150
00:26:26.857 --> 00:26:28.297
and never stopped moving.

151
00:26:28.377 --> 00:26:30.617
By now, it was like a moving bonfire.

152
00:26:34.297 --> 00:26:37.473
Didn't know if the truck
was going to explode or what.

153
00:26:40.557 --> 00:26:43.637
Still hear the man screaming.

154
00:26:48.277 --> 00:26:51.277
This thing is just backing away from it.

155
00:26:54.117 --> 00:26:59.477
I looked back at the diner to see if
there was anyone there who could help me.

156
00:27:01.617 --> 00:27:06.317
That was when I noticed that the
entire place had been encircled.

157
00:27:08.397 --> 00:27:11.997
There wasn't a sign of life left except...

158
00:27:15.137 --> 00:27:17.397
By now there were no more screams.

159
00:27:19.437 --> 00:27:21.777
I realized that...

160
00:27:22.577 --> 00:27:27.557
I was alone with 50 or
60 of those things, just

161
00:27:27.637 --> 00:27:32.597
standing there, staring at me.

162
00:27:34.417 --> 00:27:36.497
I started to drive.

163
00:27:37.637 --> 00:27:39.977
I just plowed right through them.

164
00:27:40.977 --> 00:27:42.237
They didn't move.

165
00:27:42.317 --> 00:27:47.737
They didn't run or just
stood there staring at me.

166
00:27:50.157 --> 00:27:52.337
Just wanted to crush them.

167
00:27:57.497 --> 00:28:01.037
They scattered through the air like bugs.

168
00:28:03.217 --> 00:28:08.377
We were riding in the
cemetery, Johnny and me.

169
00:28:09.337 --> 00:28:10.617
Johnny.

170
00:28:16.257 --> 00:28:21.457
We came to put a wreath
on my father's grave.

171
00:28:23.677 --> 00:28:25.157
Johnny and...

172
00:28:25.237 --> 00:28:27.397
And he said,

173
00:28:27.897 --> 00:28:30.177
Can I have some candy,

174
00:28:30.737 --> 00:28:31.737
Barbara?

175
00:28:34.337 --> 00:28:36.677
And we didn't have any.

176
00:28:40.057 --> 00:28:41.237
And...

177
00:28:44.257 --> 00:28:46.737
Oh, it's hot in here.

178
00:28:46.917 --> 00:28:48.097
Hot.

179
00:28:54.457 --> 00:28:58.097
And he said, oh, it's late.

180
00:28:58.177 --> 00:29:00.657
Why did we start so late?

181
00:29:02.977 --> 00:29:08.037
Johnny, if you'd gotten up
earlier, we wouldn't be late.

182
00:29:09.137 --> 00:29:11.957
Johnny asked me if I were afraid.

183
00:29:12.237 --> 00:29:15.777
And I said, I'm not afraid, Johnny.

184
00:29:17.217 --> 00:29:21.317
And then this man started
walking up the road.

185
00:29:22.357 --> 00:29:28.917
He came slowly, and Johnny kept teasing
me and saying, he's coming to get you,

186
00:29:28.997 --> 00:29:29.997
Barbara.

187
00:29:30.257 --> 00:29:33.777
And I laughed at him and
said, Johnny, stop it.

188
00:29:34.477 --> 00:29:37.097
And then Johnny ran away.

189
00:29:37.297 --> 00:29:42.757
And I went up to this man,
and I was going to apologize.

190
00:29:43.757 --> 00:29:46.097
Why don't you just keep calm?

191
00:29:46.217 --> 00:29:49.737
And I looked up, and I said, could he?

192
00:29:51.017 --> 00:29:52.977
And he grabbed me!

193
00:29:53.657 --> 00:29:55.497
He grabbed me!

194
00:29:55.777 --> 00:29:57.177
And he ripped at me!

195
00:29:57.257 --> 00:30:01.197
He helped me and he ripped at my clothes.

196
00:30:01.277 --> 00:30:03.337
I think you should just calm down.

197
00:30:03.477 --> 00:30:06.477
Oh, I screamed, Johnny!

198
00:30:06.557 --> 00:30:08.277
Johnny, help me!

199
00:30:08.357 --> 00:30:10.217
Oh, help me!

200
00:30:10.357 --> 00:30:12.617
And he wouldn't let me go.

201
00:30:12.697 --> 00:30:14.097
He ripped...

202
00:30:15.257 --> 00:30:20.337
And then Johnny came and he
ran and he fought this man.

203
00:30:20.417 --> 00:30:24.397
And I got so afraid, I ran.

204
00:30:24.477 --> 00:30:26.037
I ran.

205
00:30:30.337 --> 00:30:32.617
And Johnny didn't come.

206
00:30:33.877 --> 00:30:35.117
We've got to...

207
00:30:35.197 --> 00:30:37.617
We have to wait for Johnny.

208
00:30:43.537 --> 00:30:46.037
We better go out and get him.

209
00:30:47.117 --> 00:30:49.557
We have to go out and get Johnny.

210
00:30:49.637 --> 00:30:51.137
He's out there.

211
00:30:52.217 --> 00:30:53.857
Please, don't you hear me?

212
00:30:53.937 --> 00:30:56.297
We've got to go out and get him.

213
00:30:57.757 --> 00:30:58.737
Please!

214
00:30:58.817 --> 00:31:01.497
We have got to go get Johnny!

215
00:31:01.577 --> 00:31:03.657
Please help me!

216
00:31:03.757 --> 00:31:04.817
Please!

217
00:31:05.757 --> 00:31:07.297
Don't you know what's going on out there?

218
00:31:07.377 --> 00:31:08.597
This is no Sunday school picnic.

219
00:31:08.677 --> 00:31:11.297
Don't you understand? My brother is alone!

220
00:31:11.377 --> 00:31:12.857
Your brother is dead.

221
00:31:12.937 --> 00:31:13.737
No!

222
00:31:13.817 --> 00:31:16.137
My brother is not dead!

223
00:32:09.357 --> 00:32:12.357
Because of the obvious threat
to untold numbers of citizens,

224
00:32:12.437 --> 00:32:16.317
and because of the crisis which is even
now developing, this radio station will

225
00:32:16.397 --> 00:32:18.437
remain on the air day and night.

226
00:32:18.517 --> 00:32:22.477
This station and hundreds of other radio
and TV stations throughout this part of the

227
00:32:22.557 --> 00:32:26.577
country are pooling their resources through
an emergency network hookup to keep you

228
00:32:26.657 --> 00:32:28.217
informed of all developments.

229
00:32:28.297 --> 00:32:31.737
At this hour, we repeat, these
are the facts as we know them.

230
00:32:31.817 --> 00:32:35.297
There is an epidemic of mass murder
being committed by a virtual army of

231
00:32:35.377 --> 00:32:36.897
unidentified assassins.

232
00:32:36.977 --> 00:32:40.397
The murders are taking place in
villages, cities, rural homes,

233
00:32:40.477 --> 00:32:44.337
and suburbs with no apparent
pattern or reason for the slayings.

234
00:32:44.417 --> 00:32:47.837
It seems to be a sudden general
explosion of mass homicide.

235
00:32:47.917 --> 00:32:50.777
We have some descriptions
of the assassins.

236
00:32:50.937 --> 00:32:53.878
Eyewitnesses say they are
ordinary-looking people.

237
00:32:54.297 --> 00:32:56.217
They appear to be in a kind of trance.

238
00:32:56.297 --> 00:32:58.417
Others describe them as being...

239
00:33:07.457 --> 00:33:11.777
So at this point, there is no really
authentic way for us to say who or what to look

240
00:33:11.857 --> 00:33:13.877
for and guard yourself against.

241
00:33:14.177 --> 00:33:15.557
Misshapen monsters.

242
00:33:16.057 --> 00:33:19.657
Reaction of law enforcement officials is
one of complete bewilderment at this hour.

243
00:33:19.737 --> 00:33:23.037
So far, we have been unable to determine

244
00:33:24.297 --> 00:33:25.597
The investigation is yet underway.

245
00:33:25.677 --> 00:33:30.137
Police, sheriff deputies, and emergency
ambulances are literally deadluched with

246
00:33:30.217 --> 00:33:33.817
calls for help. The scene can
best be described as mayhem.

247
00:33:33.897 --> 00:33:37.857
Mayors of Pittsburgh, Philadelphia, and
Miami, along with the governors of several

248
00:33:37.937 --> 00:33:42.197
eastern and midwestern states, have indicated
the National Guard may be mobilized at

249
00:33:42.277 --> 00:33:44.297
any moment, but that
has not happened as yet.

250
00:33:44.377 --> 00:33:49.117
The only advice our reporters have been
able to get from official sources is for

251
00:33:49.197 --> 00:33:53.137
private citizens to stay in
their homes behind locked doors.

252
00:33:54.297 --> 00:33:58.317
for any reason until the nature of this
crisis has been determined and until we can

253
00:33:58.397 --> 00:34:00.457
advise what course of action to take.

254
00:34:00.537 --> 00:34:05.797
Keep listening to radio and TV for any
special instructions as this crisis develops

255
00:34:05.877 --> 00:34:06.877
further.

256
00:34:07.117 --> 00:34:11.157
Thousands of office and factory workers
are being urged to stay at their places of

257
00:34:11.237 --> 00:34:14.537
employment, not to make any
attempt to get to their homes.

258
00:34:14.617 --> 00:34:18.657
However, in spite of this urging and warning,
